description: Enforces modern Java 21+ and Micronaut 4+ standards, AOT compilation, reflection-free DI, Micronaut Data JPA, and GraalVM native image readiness.
globs: ["**/*.java", "**/application*.yml", "**/build.gradle*", "**/pom.xml"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Java & Micronaut 4+ Standards (Cursor Rules)

## 🚫 Negative Constraints (NEVER DO)
- NEVER import Spring Framework packages (`org.springframework.*`, `@Service`, `@Autowired`, `@Component`, `@RestController`).
- NEVER use field injection (`@Inject private Service s;`). Always use constructor injection with `final` fields.
- NEVER use legacy `javax.*` packages. Use `jakarta.*` exclusively (`jakarta.inject.*`, `jakarta.persistence.*`, `jakarta.validation.*`).
- NEVER block the Netty event loop. Always offload blocking I/O using `@ExecuteOn(TaskExecutors.BLOCKING)` or Java 21+ Virtual Threads (`thread-selection: AUTO`).
- NEVER rely on runtime reflection or runtime proxy generation (CGLIB). Everything must be resolvable at compile-time for GraalVM Native Image compatibility.
- NEVER return `null` from service or repository methods. Return `Optional<T>` or immutable collections (`List.of()`, `Set.of()`).

## 🧩 Dependency Injection & Architecture
- Annotate singletons with `jakarta.inject.Singleton`.
- Provide explicit constructors for dependency injection:
  ```java
  @Singleton
  public class FleetService {
      private final AssetRepository assetRepository;

      public FleetService(AssetRepository assetRepository) {
          this.assetRepository = assetRepository;
      }
  }
  ```
- For third-party beans, create a `@Factory` class with `@Singleton` producer methods.

## 🌐 HTTP Controllers & DTOs
- Use `@Controller("/api/...")` from `io.micronaut.http.annotation.Controller`.
- Return `HttpResponse<T>` with explicit HTTP status codes (`HttpResponse.ok()`, `HttpResponse.created()`, `HttpResponse.notFound()`).
- Use Java Records for request and response DTOs.
- For POJO DTOs, always add `@Introspected` or `@Serdeable` to generate compile-time serialization metadata without reflection.
- Validate inputs using `jakarta.validation.Valid` and standard constraint annotations (`@NotNull`, `@Size`, `@NotBlank`).

## 🗄️ Micronaut Data JPA
- Extend `JpaRepository<Entity, ID>` or `CrudRepository<Entity, ID>` with `@Repository`.
- Rely on compile-time query derivation methods validated during `javac` compilation.
- Prevent N+1 queries using declarative `@Join(value = "relation", type = Join.Type.FETCH)` annotations.
- Use Java Text Blocks (`"""`) for JPQL `@Query` projections with constructor expressions:
  ```java
  @Query("""
      SELECT new com.example.dto.SummaryDTO(e.id, e.name, o.title)
      FROM Entity e LEFT JOIN e.owner o WHERE e.status = :status
  """)
  List<SummaryDTO> findSummaries(Status status);
  ```
- Apply `jakarta.transaction.Transactional` on state modifications, `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` on read operations.

## 🧪 Testing with @MicronautTest
- Annotate test classes with `@MicronautTest` using JUnit 5.
- Inject dependencies via constructor injection, test method arguments, or `@Inject` on test fields.
- Use AssertJ (`assertThat(...)`) for assertions.

## 🔄 Self-Correction Verification
- Run `./gradlew compileJava` or `mvn compile` to verify Micronaut annotation processors pass.
- Run `./gradlew test` or `mvn test` to verify unit and integration tests.
